2026-06-01 11:10:38,030 - INFO - Rep 2: Generated argument: Subsidizing investigative journalism is essential to a healthy democracy. Deep reporting uncovers corruption, fraud, and abuses of power that markets alone often fail to support because such work is expensive, slow, and risky. When local newsrooms collapse, wrongdoing flourishes in the dark and citizens lose the information they need to hold leaders accountable. Carefully designed public subsidies can protect editorial independence through transparent, arms-length funding mechanisms. Supporting investigative journalism is not charity; it is civic infrastructure, as vital to self-government as courts, elections, and public records.
